00:18:04.840 --> 00:18:10.120
competitions, with skydiving canopies, we're flying

00:18:10.120 --> 00:18:14.320
paragliders, you know, and I often used an Alpine climbing

00:18:14.320 --> 00:18:19.200
analogy in paragliding and in Alpine climbing, the alpinist is

00:18:19.200 --> 00:18:22.800
trying to do the most with the least, you know, small teams,

00:18:23.200 --> 00:18:29.240
single push, minimal gear and moving as fast and as light as

00:18:29.240 --> 00:18:34.480
possible to achieve incredible objectives.

00:18:35.560 --> 00:18:41.800
And I feel like in air sport, the paraglider is exactly the

00:18:41.800 --> 00:18:49.160
mirror of the alpinist and we have the lightest and the most

00:18:49.160 --> 00:18:57.120
compact and the simplest of aircraft and we do incredible

00:18:57.120 --> 00:18:59.200
things with them, mind blowing things.

00:18:59.840 --> 00:19:04.920
And we're literally doing the most with the least in terms of

00:19:04.960 --> 00:19:10.720
air sport in my opinion. And so in with that comes risk.

00:19:10.760 --> 00:19:16.160
You know, we have the, we have the smallest operating envelope

00:19:16.720 --> 00:19:23.200
and we tend to try to operate in the most extreme mountain

00:19:23.200 --> 00:19:28.000
environments with the aircraft with the smallest operating

00:19:28.120 --> 00:19:34.680
envelope, you know, the most with the least and amazing

00:19:34.840 --> 00:19:38.040
feasts have been achieved every year.

00:19:38.240 --> 00:19:45.240
It's mind blowing to me on what pilots do with paragliders in

00:19:45.240 --> 00:19:48.240
terms of pushing the boundaries of what is possible.

00:19:48.640 --> 00:19:51.800
It's incredible. So on.

00:19:52.000 --> 00:19:59.120
But safety on is the thing that is the most difficult to manage

00:19:59.520 --> 00:20:03.880
because you are trying to be as safe as possible with the least

00:20:03.880 --> 00:20:08.480
capable. The least stable of all the

00:20:08.480 --> 00:20:13.600
aircraft that you could be flying except maybe a skydiving

00:20:13.600 --> 00:20:16.280
canopy, which you're not going to be flying across country.

00:20:16.800 --> 00:20:22.720
So I think at times were unrealistic as to what can be

00:20:22.720 --> 00:20:26.000
achieved safety wise, even though I do think incremental

00:20:26.000 --> 00:20:29.280
gains can be made. If we really wanted to be safe,

00:20:29.840 --> 00:20:35.200
safer in a tangible way like many pilots have done, they

00:20:35.200 --> 00:20:39.040
switched to sailplanes and sailplanes, you know, it's more

00:20:39.280 --> 00:20:44.360
robust, capable aircraft with more performance and a better

00:20:44.360 --> 00:20:47.640
safety record certainly than we have.

00:20:48.040 --> 00:20:53.560
Because now you have something that is simply more capable with

00:20:53.560 --> 00:21:01.800
a larger operating envelope and, and you can mitigate a lot of

00:21:01.800 --> 00:21:08.480
risk that can haunt you or push you out of flying paragliders

00:21:08.800 --> 00:21:10.480
and still enjoy being in the air.

00:21:10.520 --> 00:21:13.960
You just move to a, you know, you move to a better aircraft

