essentially. And many pilots have and they've

00:21:18.200 --> 00:21:24.720
extended their flying careers or at least pursuits by switching

00:21:24.720 --> 00:21:28.680
to sailplanes from either hang gliders or paragliders because

00:21:28.680 --> 00:21:32.000
they were no longer down for managing the risk.

00:21:33.040 --> 00:21:37.480
And so, so that's one way to do it if you want to mitigate risk.

00:21:37.560 --> 00:21:42.840
But if we're within the sport itself and you want to add

00:21:42.840 --> 00:21:51.080
regulation, the first place to start is testing requirements.

00:21:51.560 --> 00:21:59.640
And so if the data supports a increase in back protection or

00:21:59.640 --> 00:22:06.320
if the data supports more robust lines, you know, for G testing

