00:44:12.400 --> 00:44:16.600
Do you understand my context? Maybe you could tell me if I've

00:44:16.600 --> 00:44:23.320
got it wrong by my answer. When the open class was banned,

00:44:23.320 --> 00:44:26.320
I quit flying competitions for a while.

00:44:26.440 --> 00:44:28.640
You know, I called it my one man protest.

00:44:28.840 --> 00:44:30.400
You know, everybody else moved on.

00:44:30.400 --> 00:44:34.760
And I was like, all right, if you're going to take away the

00:44:34.760 --> 00:44:38.200
open class, which I felt was critical to glider development,

00:44:38.320 --> 00:44:42.760
to technology development on all the factory pilots that you

00:44:42.760 --> 00:44:50.360
competed against had prototypes of what the future could

00:44:50.360 --> 00:44:53.800
potentially hold that they were trying to validate one way or

00:44:53.800 --> 00:44:58.800
the other. And while, you know, you felt

00:44:58.800 --> 00:45:01.760
like you weren't ever going to be competitive against those

00:45:01.760 --> 00:45:08.320
factory pilots on the next greatest thing, I was as a

00:45:08.320 --> 00:45:19.200
