00:45:19.200 --> 00:45:21.680
would in the long run benefit the sport.

00:45:23.040 --> 00:45:28.320
And many of those ideas are now in, you know, being sea gliders

00:45:29.040 --> 00:45:36.120
and also in kite surfing planks. And they were all developed on

00:45:36.880 --> 00:45:43.920
via the open class. And and so now on we've, you

00:45:43.920 --> 00:45:50.400
know, I felt like, you know, the analogy I was using was now

00:45:50.400 --> 00:45:54.840
we're go Kart racing. And so before we were only using

00:45:54.840 --> 00:45:58.040
top speed in the straightaway. And now you just fly.

00:45:58.320 --> 00:46:00.920
Now you're just going around the track with your pedal to the

00:46:00.920 --> 00:46:07.600
floor all the time because you're, you know, the speed has

00:46:07.600 --> 00:46:10.240
been limited. And so now everybody's flying,

00:46:10.320 --> 00:46:13.760
you know, at the same top speed and we're just all racing around

00:46:13.760 --> 00:46:16.160
the track, you know, with our foot to the floor.

00:46:17.120 --> 00:46:24.240
And I felt like we were punishing guys like Josh or, you

00:46:24.240 --> 00:46:27.560
know, Kriegel or any of the luminaries, you know, back in

00:46:27.560 --> 00:46:30.160
the day that were really good at keeping their gliders open.

00:46:30.160 --> 00:46:33.760
We were taking away something that they were good at because

00:46:33.760 --> 00:46:39.280
all of us weren't good at it. And so now we were taking, you

00:46:39.280 --> 00:46:45.360
know, their talent and their advantage off the field and

00:46:45.960 --> 00:46:51.080
making it a better race for us mortals and a worse race for

00:46:51.080 --> 00:46:56.440
them. But you know, after, you know, a

00:46:56.440 --> 00:47:00.960
decade plus, you know, because I only just got an Enzo 3 last

